  "notes": {
    "c0001.md": "# Priya Nakamura / Fairview Commons HOA\n\nSigned two years ago at $1,450 a month. The contract has a price review\nclause that has never once been invoked, by either side.\n\n- July: comfortably profitable.\n- August: thin.\n- September: lost money for the first time.\n\nCrew cost on this route is up about 25 percent since signing. Fuel is up too.\nThe invoice always gets paid on time - that was never the issue. The number on\nthe invoice is the issue.\n",
    "p0003.md": "# Fairview Commons - September grounds contract\n\nRed. Revenue 1,450, same as every month for two years. Crew cost 1,075 this\nmonth against 870 in July. Fuel and materials up too. Net loss on the route for\nthe first time.\n\nThis is not a collections problem - Priya pays like clockwork. It is a pricing\nproblem: nobody put \"review the contract\" on any list, so it never happened.\n\nNext: send the rate letter before the October invoice goes out, or drop a crew\nhour off the route.\n"
  }
